[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2925407318","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-2925407318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":2925407318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uXixW","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T16:28:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T16:28:34Z","body":"Are these cosmetic errors or are the properties lost / affecting the releasable game?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2925407318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2926329382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-2926329382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":2926329382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ubD4m","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-01T02:50:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-01T02:50:16Z","body":"> Are these cosmetic errors or are the properties lost / affecting the releasable game?\n\nThey appear to be cosmetic.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2926329382/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828202947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-3828202947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":3828202947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kLb3D","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T11:40:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T11:40:10Z","body":"I'm getting a similar error when trying to create a new MultiMesh in a gltf extension, also cosmetic:\n\n```gdscript\nvar multimesh = MultiMesh.new()\nmultimesh.instance_count = 0\nmultimesh.transform_format = MultiMesh.TRANSFORM_3D\nmultimesh.instance_count = instance_count\n```\n\n<img width=\"625\" height=\"111\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/201a4f10-c85c-47a5-ab04-f90a9fdf47a5\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828202947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828234234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-3828234234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":3828234234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kLjf6","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T11:53:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T11:53:38Z","body":"I don't reproduce the issue with your code snippet @passivestar.\n\nLooking at the MultiMesh code, I don't see how it could trigger this warning if you explicitly set `instance_count = 0` just before setting `transform_format`. The setters seem to be change the values immediately so there shouldn't be any deferred behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828234234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828250629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-3828250629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":3828250629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kLngF","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T11:58:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T12:28:50Z","body":"I do reproduce the issue with @MajorMcDoom's MRP on the other hand.\n\nThis likely happens because when loading the scene, the various properties are set in an order that doesn't guarantee that `instance_count` is set last.\n\nThere should probably be a dirty/uninitialized flag on load that lets one set these properties in any order (whatever happens when loading the scene) and only then call `RenderingServer::get_singleton()->multimesh_allocate_data()` once the init is finalized. That doesn't seem trivial though, there's a lot of stuff in there that depends on being called in the right order.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828250629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828402207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-3828402207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":3828402207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kMMgf","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T12:41:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T12:41:16Z","body":"> I don't reproduce the issue with your code snippet @passivestar.\n\nI guess the problem is somewhere else then. I made an mrp: [mrpmm.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24982254/mrpmm.zip)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/84754114-4789-4c9e-8891-e7802572a857","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828402207/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501350659","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-4501350659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":4501350659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDE0pAw","user":{"login":"Rouli-M","id":20565757,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTY1NzU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20565757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M","html_url":"https://github.com/Rouli-M","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rouli-M/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T18:20:41Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T18:20:41Z","body":"Facing the same issue. My quick dumb workaround is just closing the parent scene to get rid of the log.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501350659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4643135722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-4643135722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":4643135722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFMCg6g","user":{"login":"alexxdann","id":17780142,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzgwMTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17780142?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann","html_url":"https://github.com/alexxdann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexxdann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-07T15:42:19Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T15:48:54Z","body":"Same issue with MultiMeshInstance2D and similar/same scenes setup as op have (use_colors in my case). Interesting thing there's no such error if MultiMeshInstance2D node is directly using in Scene A.\n\nAnyway for now I can see only workaround to avoid it, i.e. disable in editor all such options, on _init of MultiMeshInstance2D/3D script temporarily set instance_count to zero, set all options you need and set incstace_count back, like this:\n\n```\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\tvar tmp_count = multimesh.instance_count;\n\tmultimesh.instance_count = 0;\n\tmultimesh.use_colors = true;\n\tmultimesh.instance_count = tmp_count;\n```\n\nIt resolved the error in my case.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4643135722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4665092716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-4665092716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":4665092716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFg-qbA","user":{"login":"Chestnut45","id":48457382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NDU3Mzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48457382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45","html_url":"https://github.com/Chestnut45","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chestnut45/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-09T23:43:13Z","updated_at":"2026-06-09T23:43:13Z","body":"Running into the same issue in 4.6.3.stable. In my case I'm already extending MultiMeshInstance3D, hiding the `multimesh` property from the inspector window, and creating a new multimesh in `_ready` anyway, so it's a fine workaround for me to just avoid serializing the multimesh property at all:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _validate_property(property: Dictionary) -> void:\n\tif property.name == \"multimesh\":\n\t\tproperty.usage = PROPERTY_USAGE_NONE\n```\n\nObviously a very limited use case, but figured it was worth sharing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4665092716/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4705725629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-4705725629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":4705725629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGHusvQ","user":{"login":"Litewhite","id":11568811,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTY4ODEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11568811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite","html_url":"https://github.com/Litewhite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Litewhite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:51:53Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T07:51:53Z","body":"Adding an early quit fixed my case: \n```cpp\nvoid MultiMesh::set_transform_format(TransformFormat p_transform_format) {\n\t// {FIX} if equal than return.\n\tif (transform_format == p_transform_format) {\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\t// {FIXend}\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(instance_count > 0, \"Instance count must be 0 to change the transform format.\");\n\ttransform_format = p_transform_format;\n}\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4705725629/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073464840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106950#issuecomment-5073464840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106950","id":5073464840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLmbuCA","user":{"login":"AALLAANN","id":28680951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjgwOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28680951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN","html_url":"https://github.com/AALLAANN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AALLAANN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T19:00:29Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T19:00:29Z","body":"I can confirm that this issue is still present in Godot 4.7.1 stable.\n\nGodot versions:\n- The problem started appearing in my project after upgrading to Godot 4.7 stable.\n- It is still reproducible in Godot 4.7.1 stable.\n- I did not encounter this behavior in my previous Godot 4.5 workflow.\n\nSystem information:\n- Windows 11 Pro, build 26200\n- Godot 4.7.1.stable.official\n- OpenGL Compatibility renderer\n- NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650, driver 32.0.15.9186\n- AMD Ryzen 5 3600\n\nMy main scene contains 62 inline MultiMesh resources. When the editor opens or reloads this scene, Godot prints the following error exactly once for every MultiMesh:\n\nERROR: Instance count must be 0 to change the transform format.\nat: set_transform_format (scene/resources/multimesh.cpp:357)\n\nIn my case, this results in 62 identical errors whenever the scene is restored by the editor.\n\nThe serialized resources originally look correct:\n\ntransform_format = 1\ninstance_count = 10\nmesh = SubResource(\"...\")\nbuffer = PackedFloat32Array(...)\n\nHowever, it appears that when the cached resource is reloaded or replaced by the editor, transform_format is assigned while the existing MultiMesh still has a non-zero instance_count.\n\nThe MultiMeshes continue rendering correctly, so the errors appear to be cosmetic, but they flood the output and make it difficult to notice real errors.\n\nI confirmed the following workaround:\n\ninstance_count = 0\ntransform_format = 1\ninstance_count = 10\nmesh = SubResource(\"...\")\nbuffer = PackedFloat32Array(...)\n\nAfter adding the initial instance_count = 0 to all 62 resources, the same project opens in Godot 4.7.1 with zero MultiMesh errors.\n\nUnfortunately, this workaround is not durable because saving the scene again in the editor may remove the additional instance_count = 0 assignment, causing the errors to return.\n\nPossible engine-side fixes:\n\n1. Reset instance_count to zero before restoring properties such as transform_format, use_colors, and use_custom_data during resource reload.\n\n2. Alternatively, the setters could return early when the requested value is already equal to the current value, before validating instance_count. For example:\n\nvoid MultiMesh::set_transform_format(TransformFormat p_transform_format) {\n    if (transform_format == p_transform_format) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n    ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(\n        instance_count > 0,\n        \"Instance count must be 0 to change the transform format.\"\n    );\n\n    transform_format = p_transform_format;\n}\n\nA similar equality check may be appropriate for use_colors and use_custom_data.\n\nThis seems related to cached MultiMesh resources being restored in an unsafe property order by the editor.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073464840/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]